AB  - Large language model (LLM)-based generative AI systems are vulnerable to jailbreak attacks, in which malicious prompts bypass safety mechanisms. This study investigates whether retrieval augmented generation (RAG)-based LLM systems are susceptible to such attacks. The effectiveness and efficiency of various defense techniques, including safety-enhanced system prompts and input/output filtering, are analyzed. The results of experiments demonstrate that RAG-based LLM systems remain vulnerable to jailbreak attacks. Implementing defense mechanisms at each stage significantly reduces attack success rates (ASRs). Specifically, safety-enhanced system prompts reduce ASRs by over 78% with minimal impact on response time, indicating high defense efficiency. Incorporating Prompt Guard as an input/output guardrail slightly increases response time but reduces ASRs by approximately 93.9%, while increasing the false positive rate by only 2%. This defense combination is the most effective in our experimental setup.
